# The vendored fixtures and the skill templates are asserted byte for byte
# against stride-lite. Git's own EOL normalization would rewrite them on a
# clone with core.autocrlf=true and break that assertion on a checkout nobody
# edited, so it is disabled here.
#
# This PREVENTS git from normalizing. It does not normalize inside the check —
# test/smoke.sh still compares raw bytes and still detects a CR, which is what
# the task's "no whitespace or line-ending normalization" rule requires.
*.md -text
fixtures/** -text
